      <div type="clause" n="46.1a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 46.1a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 46.1a" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="570" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si lex domino uadietur, differat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="p" target="#Hn_46-1a.lnote.oe.p"/> cetera placita, donec lex deducatur per burgi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="q" target="#Hn_46-1a.lnote.oe.q"/> legem — nisi de furto uel capitalibus sit, in quibus statim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="r" target="#Hn_46-1a.lnote.oe.r"/> oportet responderi.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 570 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_46-1a.lnote.oe.p" n="p" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">570</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gerichtsherr</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lord of the court</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_46-1a.lnote.oe.q" n="q" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">570</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= curiae; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 38</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= curiae; cf. 38</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_46-1a.lnote.oe.r" n="r" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">570</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 9, 2. 46, 3. 47. 49, 1. 52, 1<hi rend="italic">b</hi>. 53, 2. 59, 3. 61, 17<hi rend="italic">f</hi>. <hi rend="italic">Achtsachen gehen bei Verbrechenskonkurrenz vor; Schreuer</hi> Verbrechenskonk. 252</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 9, 2. 46, 3. 47. 49, 1. 52, 1<hi rend="italic">b</hi>. 53, 2. 59, 3. 61, 17<hi rend="italic">f</hi>. Where offences concur, cases involving outlawry take precedence; Schreuer Verbrechenskonk. 252</seg></note>
      </div>
